# Orchestrator lead (model-tier delegation)

When driving **`workflow_step`** as the **lead session**, pass your active model tier in state so pnCore can adapt orchestration vs implementation:

| State key | Type | Role |
|-----------|------|------|
| **`leadModelTier`** | `fast` \| `standard` \| `premium` \| `premium_thinking` \| `long_horizon` | Preferred — declare the tier matching your picker model |
| **`sessionModel`** | string | Optional picker slug; resolved via exemplars/alternates from `suggest_model_tier` / `pn-core://reference/subagent-routing.md` |
| **`orchestrationIntent`** | boolean | Opt-in delegation before parallel fan-out: `long_horizon` → `lead`; premium → `light_delegate`; standard + parallel → `light_delegate` |

Echo these on **every** `workflow_step` call in the same run (with `run_id`). Full delegation contracts appear when **`parallel: true`** or **`orchestrationIntent: true`** (including non-parallel steps when intent is set).

## When `workflow_step` returns `orchestrationMode`

| Mode | Lead behavior |
|------|----------------|
| **`lead`** | `long_horizon` declared — plan, coordinate, verify only; **no bulk file edits** in lead session |
| **`light_delegate`** | Premium + (`parallel` or `orchestrationIntent`), or `orchestrationIntent` + `parallel` on standard — spawn Task subagents per `tasks[]`; lead may fix ≤1 trivial file |
| **`implementer`** | Default — lead may implement directly |

## Delegation contract

1. Read **`subagentTierHints`** and **`tasks[].suggestedSubagentTier`** on the response.
2. For each parallel task, spawn **Task** (`generalPurpose`, `best-of-n-runner`, `explore`, `shell`) with `model` set to the **builder** or **explorer** exemplar from hints — not the lead model.
3. Call **`suggest_model_tier`** with `role: "orchestrator"` at session start for the recommended long-horizon exemplar (default: Fable; alternates in `TIER_META`).
4. Re-call **`workflow_step`** only after all delegated tasks report summaries in `taskResults`.
5. After **two verification failures** on the same finding, record in loop STATE and follow `pn-core://reference/loop-catalog/escalation-queue.md`.

## Without long_horizon access

Set `PNCORE_FEATURES` or `features.json`: `"tierAliases": { "long_horizon": "premium" }` — **lead mode behavior is unchanged**; only the exemplar string downgrades.

Pair with `pn-core://reference/subagent-routing.md` and `pn-core://reference/loop-orchestration-guide.md`.
